' FactStamp - PERT Chart (Program Evaluation and Review Technique)
' Chapter 3.3 - Planning and Scheduling
' Build:  plantuml -tsvg pert_chart.puml
'
' The schedule is a strictly linear chain of eight 2-week sprints executed by a
' single developer, so EVERY activity lies on the critical path and every
' activity has zero slack. Critical path length = 8 x 2 wks = 16 weeks.
'
' PlantUML has no native PERT notation, so the network is expressed with the
' primitives it does have: an ellipse for each START/END milestone, a rectangle
' for each activity node, and labelled arrows for the precedence edges. The
' whole network is a single vertical chain, per the portrait-page rule.

@startuml
skinparam style strictuml
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam defaultFontName "Liberation Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 20
skinparam defaultFontStyle bold
skinparam titleFontSize 26
skinparam titleFontStyle bold
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam ArrowColor black
skinparam ArrowThickness 2.5
skinparam ArrowFontSize 17
skinparam ArrowFontStyle bold
skinparam RectangleBorderColor black
skinparam RectangleBorderThickness 2.5
skinparam RectangleBackgroundColor #F8F9FA
skinparam RectangleFontSize 20
skinparam RectangleFontStyle bold
title FactStamp - PERT Chart

' Layout tuning: the chain is 10 nodes deep, so tighten rank spacing to stop the
' SVG stretching into an unusably thin ribbon on an A4 portrait page.
skinparam ranksep 22
skinparam nodesep 22

' Completed activities (S1-S7): solid heavy border, light background.
skinparam rectangle<<Done>> {
  BorderStyle solid
  BorderThickness 2.5
  BackgroundColor #F8F9FA
}

' Activity still in flight (S8): heavy DASHED border + darker fill, so the
' distinction survives both greyscale printing and the monochrome skinparam.
skinparam rectangle<<Underway>> {
  BorderStyle dashed
  BorderThickness 4
  BackgroundColor #D0D0D0
}

' START / END milestones: ellipse nodes, heavy border.
skinparam usecase<<Milestone>> {
  BorderThickness 4
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  FontSize 20
  FontStyle bold
}

skinparam legendFontSize 18
skinparam legendFontStyle bold
skinparam legendBackgroundColor #F8F9FA
skinparam legendBorderColor black
skinparam legendBorderThickness 2.5

' ------------------------------------------------------------------ milestones
usecase "START\nWeek 0 (01 Jun)" as START <<Milestone>>
usecase "END\nWeek 16 (30 Sep)" as END <<Milestone>>

' --------------------------------------------------------------------- sprints
' Label lines: short name / calendar slot + earliest start-finish + slack.
' Status (Done / Underway) is carried by the stereotype and the border style.
rectangle "S1: Scaffolding + Auth\nJun wk 1-2 | ES 0 - EF 2  |  Slack 0" as S1 <<Done>>
rectangle "S2: Ingestion + OCR\nJun wk 3-4 | ES 2 - EF 4  |  Slack 0" as S2 <<Done>>
rectangle "S3: Duplicate Detection\nJul wk 1-2 | ES 4 - EF 6  |  Slack 0" as S3 <<Done>>
rectangle "S4: Verification Queue\nJul wk 3-4 | ES 6 - EF 8  |  Slack 0" as S4 <<Done>>
rectangle "S5: Consensus Engine\nAug wk 1-2 | ES 8 - EF 10  |  Slack 0" as S5 <<Done>>
rectangle "S6: Cards + Analytics\nAug wk 3-4 | ES 10 - EF 12  |  Slack 0" as S6 <<Done>>
rectangle "S7: Security + Admin\nSep wk 1-2 | ES 12 - EF 14  |  Slack 0" as S7 <<Done>>
rectangle "S8: Hardening + Deploy\nSep wk 3-4 | ES 14 - EF 16  |  Slack 0" as S8 <<Underway>>

' ----------------------------------------------------- critical path (all of it)
' Every edge is on the critical path; there is no non-critical branch to draw.
START --> S1 : 2 wks
S1 --> S2 : 2 wks
S2 --> S3 : 2 wks
S3 --> S4 : 2 wks
S4 --> S5 : 2 wks
S5 --> S6 : 2 wks
S6 --> S7 : 2 wks
S7 --> S8 : 2 wks
S8 --> END : 0 wks

legend bottom
Critical Path: START -> S1 -> S2 -> S3 -> S4 -> S5 -> S6 -> S7 -> S8 -> END
Length = 16 weeks | Slack = 0 on every activity
<<Done>> solid border (S1-S7)  |  <<Underway>> dashed border, shaded (S8)
end legend

@enduml
